<p>The French constrained writing group Oulipo invented a new crime they call &#8220;plagiarism by anticipation.&#8221;</p>
<p>If William Shakespeare writes something, and you later write the same thing, then Shakespeare is guilty of plagiarism for anticipating your idea.</p>
<p>&#8220;Thus justice is done, and each is rewarded according to his merit.&#8221;</p>
